{
  "bridge_text": "The secret of the firefly's fate remains tucked away, but we shall see what happens as the mossy glow begins to flicker once more.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs the humming was a quiet song, and a firefly the size of a robin lay on a bed of moss. Her glow was almost out. Mosk's whiskers trembled as he remembered how he had failed to bring her medicine one winter long ago. He had been guarding the tree ever since, far too ashamed to face his old friend until this very moment."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt and asked the firefly queen what she needed. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, said the queen, that was all medicine ever was. Mosk fetched the milk in a thimble and laid his paw beside hers. The queen's glow steadied. The humming inside the tree turned into a tune Lina had not heard before — and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The apple sat heavy and bright on the wooden step, a small peace offering as the forest grew still around them. Mosk finally moved, his shadow stretching long toward the path that led deeper into the hollow.",
